  "caveats": [
    "Paper bandwidth 111.774 MHz is internally inconsistent: 490.359 minus 379.585 = 110.774 MHz. Preserve reported value and derived subtraction separately. Retained bandwidth expression computes edge difference.",
    "Abstract says K exceeds 115 across 1 MHz\u20131 GHz; body only guarantees K>1 over sweep and gives K\u2248115.72 at 433 MHz. Use body criterion for broad-band minimum, not K_min>=115.",
    "PAE claims need audit: with global Psat 50.5 mW and stated PDC 315.34 mW, peak 42.3% cannot follow stated PAE formula if PDC is fixed; even zero-input upper bound is only about 16.0%. Retained HB computes power from current at each drive, so retain 42.3 as disputed reported reference, not automatic verified acceptance.",
    "Paper emitter drop 0.657 V over 25 ohm implies 26.28 mA emitter current, distinct from claimed 24.59 mA collector current; retained IC measures choke branch current.",
    "Paper claims originate from nominal schematic study, not retained nine T/F/S by -40/27/100 C corners.",
    "Paper HB sweep is -40 to +20 dBm in 0.1 dB steps. Retained input.scs uses start=-40 stop=20 lin=600 with 25 harmonics; this is compatible in range and nominal resolution, but extrema still depend on sampling and sizing.",
    "Later PA1088 case studies are generation-61 optimization evidence, not primary-paper results or necessarily retained sizing (case-study Q0 multiplier 11 vs retained Q0.m=10)."
  ],
